description:
Fences in the bundled languages and their aliases are highlighted; fences in an unknown language or none stay plain. The conversation /c/{{SLUG}} was started with a message whose markdown has nine fenced code blocks, which the predictable model answers with. window.__block(i) is the reply's i-th "pre > code" element (0-based; the reply being the last ".message-agent"), and eval window.__scrollToBlock(i) (it returns "scrolled") disarms auto-follow with a wheel event and scrolls block i to the middle of the view. "Block i has tokens" means eval window.__block(i).querySelector('.shelley-code-token') !== null returns true (allow 30s: highlighting runs once the block is in view). The highlighted blocks, with their exact class attribute and exact textContent (as JSON strings: each ends in a newline): Block 0: class exactly "language-elixir", source "answer = 42
". Block 1: class exactly "language-haskell", source "answer :: Int
answer = 42
". Block 2: class exactly "language-zig", source "const answer: i32 = 42;
". Block 3: class exactly "language-Dockerfile", source "FROM alpine:latest
". Block 4: class exactly "language-nix", source "answer = 42;
". Block 5: class exactly "language-clojure", source "(def answer 42)
". Block 6: class exactly "language-clj", source "(def alias-answer 42)
". 1. Navigate to /c/{{SLUG}}. 2. Eval window.__block(8) !== null && window.__block(9) === null: it must return true (exactly nine blocks; allow 30s). 3. For each highlighted block i from 0 to 6, in order: eval window.__block(i).className, which must return exactly its class; eval window.__scrollToBlock(i); block i has tokens; eval window.__block(i).textContent === S, S being its source as a JavaScript string literal, which must return true. 4. Eval window.__scrollToBlock(7), then window.__scrollToBlock(8): so that "no tokens" below means the highlighter declined them, not that it never looked. 5. Eval window.__block(7).className: exactly "language-unknown-language". 6. Eval window.__block(8).getAttribute('class') === null: true (the unlabeled fence has no class at all). 7. Eval window.__block(7).textContent === "leave_this_plain();
": true. 8. Eval window.__block(8).textContent === "also_plain();
": true. 9. Eval window.__block(7).querySelectorAll('.shelley-code-token').length: exactly "0". 10. Eval window.__block(8).querySelectorAll('.shelley-code-token').length: exactly "0". 11. Eval window.__scrollToBlock(0); block 0 has tokens. 12. In one eval without "expect", record window.__tokenCount = window.__block(0).querySelectorAll('.shelley-code-token').length and window.__lightColor = getComputedStyle(window.__block(0).querySelector('.shelley-code-token')).color. 13. Eval document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', true), switching to the dark theme. 14. Eval getComputedStyle(window.__block(0).querySelector('.shelley-code-token')).color !== window.__lightColor until it returns true: the tokens recolor. 15. Eval window.__block(0).querySelectorAll('.shelley-code-token').length === window.__tokenCount: true (recoloring does not re-tokenize).
